1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,964
The system is built around one deterministic core.

2
00:00:03,964 --> 00:00:07,294
A business brief and a DDSP package enter.

3
00:00:07,294 --> 00:00:09,910
The parser normalizes the schema.

4
00:00:09,910 --> 00:00:15,301
The planner, and only the planner, is inside the narrow AI boundary.

5
00:00:15,301 --> 00:00:19,344
It produces a typed document contract, never OOXML.

6
00:00:19,344 --> 00:00:23,445
The contract then takes two paths: validation and preview.

7
00:00:23,445 --> 00:00:29,808
If structural, semantic and logical checks pass, the compiler writes a deterministic DOCX.

8
00:00:29,808 --> 00:00:35,040
Preview and DOCX share the same structure, so they cannot drift by design.

9
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:41,634
The parser reads the DDSP package, validates its XML boundaries and normalizes controls into a schema.

10
00:00:41,634 --> 00:00:45,384
Types, collection scope and sample values become explicit.

11
00:00:45,384 --> 00:00:53,400
Every later stage sees the same normalized view, so a path cannot mean one thing to the planner and another to the compiler.

12
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,480
A request is a sequence of narrow contracts.

13
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:59,699
The web app, CLI or API calls TemplateService.

14
00:00:59,699 --> 00:01:09,498
Planning gets schema evidence and the brief; validation gets the typed template; compilation gets only a validated template and sample data.

15
00:01:09,498 --> 00:01:12,648
A blocking report returns without a document.

16
00:01:12,648 --> 00:01:16,473
In the live demo, the brief is split into requirements.

17
00:01:16,473 --> 00:01:23,359
Candidate fields carry type and scope; the reviewer sees confirmed, ambiguous and missing bindings.

18
00:01:23,359 --> 00:01:26,280
The planner cannot bind arbitrary strings.

19
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,893
The preview is not a screenshot of Word.

20
00:01:28,893 --> 00:01:33,596
It is an independent renderer that consumes the same template structure.

21
00:01:33,596 --> 00:01:41,304
That gives the reviewer a fast, visible check of order, hierarchy and conditional content before downloading the DOCX.

22
00:01:41,304 --> 00:01:45,732
The contract is a small typed model: document, sections, blocks.

23
00:01:45,732 --> 00:01:49,744
Tables carry repeated rows, row templates and footer rows.

24
00:01:49,744 --> 00:01:57,216
Repeats carry a path and alias; conditions carry typed expressions; images carry source and fallback policy.

25
00:01:57,216 --> 00:01:59,590
Every block has one legal shape.

26
00:01:59,590 --> 00:02:02,187
Paragraphs and headings carry runs.

27
00:02:02,187 --> 00:02:05,674
Tables own their rows and optional footer rows.

28
00:02:05,674 --> 00:02:08,715
Repeats and conditions own nested blocks.

29
00:02:08,715 --> 00:02:12,722
Images carry source, fallback and aspect-ratio policy.

30
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:18,360
The validator can check those rules because they are types, not conventions.

31
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,966
Validation is layered.

32
00:02:19,966 --> 00:02:22,740
Structural checks reject malformed IR.

33
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:26,608
Semantic checks reject unknown or incompatible paths.

34
00:02:26,608 --> 00:02:32,229
Logical checks enforce collection scope, condition types and image placement.

35
00:02:32,229 --> 00:02:34,200
V1 to V3 block compilation.

36
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:41,280
Visual checks use sample data; compatibility with Docentric AX remains a separate untreated gate.

37
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:46,357
After the blocking gate, the visual check uses sample data when it is available.

38
00:02:46,357 --> 00:02:50,101
The compatibility level is separate and remains not tested.

39
00:02:50,101 --> 00:02:58,224
That distinction matters: a valid generic DOCX is not a claim that the document will run inside a third-party reporting runtime.

40
00:02:58,224 --> 00:02:59,893
The compiler owns OOXML.

41
00:02:59,893 --> 00:03:07,265
It resolves relationships, writes real sections, headers and footers, embeds media and normalizes the ZIP.

42
00:03:07,265 --> 00:03:13,872
The output has stable ordering and fixed timestamps, so the same inputs produce the same bytes.

43
00:03:13,872 --> 00:03:16,573
First-page headers are real Word parts.

44
00:03:16,573 --> 00:03:20,659
The section sets titlePg and points to a first-page header.

45
00:03:20,659 --> 00:03:23,983
Later sections can inherit a header or clear it.

46
00:03:23,983 --> 00:03:30,216
That is why the logo appears once, while the company identity stays in the default header.

47
00:03:30,216 --> 00:03:35,155
Table inference reads bounded geometry and joins it to schema evidence.

48
00:03:35,155 --> 00:03:42,737
It handles static headers, repeated rows, optional conditional cells, footer rows and a tested nested repeat.

49
00:03:42,737 --> 00:03:46,632
Merged or ambiguous tables are refused with diagnostics.

50
00:03:46,632 --> 00:03:51,432
Images support schema data, static assets, fallback and aspect ratio.

51
00:03:51,432 --> 00:03:55,081
Reference evaluation is separate from semantic quality.

52
00:03:55,081 --> 00:03:59,792
Seventeen official documents parse, sixteen import and fifteen compile.

53
00:03:59,792 --> 00:04:06,096
The two residual failures are an unenclosed nested collection and an unsupported-only document.

54
00:04:06,096 --> 00:04:13,594
Thirty observed tables are classified: fifteen accepted, fifteen deliberately unsupported, zero silently dropped.

55
00:04:13,594 --> 00:04:18,504
The pipeline counts are deliberately separate from the semantic benchmark.

56
00:04:18,504 --> 00:04:26,087
The semantic benchmark runs thirty-two cases across three providers and three repeats, with technical failures separated.

57
00:04:26,087 --> 00:04:29,095
Two hundred seventy-four runs pass semantically.

58
00:04:29,095 --> 00:04:37,179
Precision is ninety-five percent; recall and F1 are higher; ten Gemini structured-output failures remain technical, not semantic.

59
00:04:37,179 --> 00:04:44,448
The report keeps the technical and semantic views separate, so a missing structured response cannot inflate quality.

60
00:04:44,448 --> 00:04:58,166
The honest limits: Word for the web still needs a manual browser check; the videos are drafts; AT-07 remains partial because the gold labels lack independent human review; and Docentric AX runtime compatibility is not tested.

61
00:04:58,166 --> 00:05:03,288
A deterministic document engine can prove the document, not somebody else's runtime.

62
00:05:03,288 --> 00:05:09,128
One deterministic core, a narrow AI boundary, and evidence at every step.

63
00:05:09,128 --> 00:05:11,208
That is Docentric Copilot.
